                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Sea Will Claim Everything is a beautiful, humanist game. It cares about moments and the joy of details, it values community and the individual. It believes that the efforts in being honest and kind (to yourself, to others, to the world around you) are true rewards. Ursula Le Guin would feel at home here, in the Lands of Dream.\n\nI recommend this game to everyone, though I'm not sure this game is *for* everyone. I think that playing it requires a high level of patience and trust, a willingness to sit still and think and sip a nice drink and maybe a lot of pauses to go and pet a cat, a love of reading 100 book titles and stopping at each one to imagine the person that would own all those books and what they must be like.\n\nI think for the people this game does hit for, it will feel momentous and vast and warm.\n—\nAlso it's now 1/10th the price it used to be, and includes all of the Land of Dreams games in one collection. I'd strongly recommend The Fabulous Screech and The Matter of the Great Red Dragon. And check out the developers audio dramas, The Gospel of the Living Flood and Azathoth Blues (neither of those are on steam, both on your podcast services of choice. And both amazing listens, in particular the voice acting and sound design and story of Azathoth Blues.)",
                        "timestamp_created": 1783279372,
